  "indications": {
    "value": "Replacement therapy for hypothyroidism (primary, secondary, tertiary) in adult and pediatric patients including neonates; adjunct to surgery and radioiodine therapy for pituitary TSH suppression in thyrotropin-dependent well-differentiated thyroid cancer. Not indicated for suppression of benign thyroid nodules or nontoxic diffuse goiter in iodine-sufficient patients, nor for hypothyroidism during recovery from subacute thyroiditis.",
    "source_quote": "Levothyroxine sodium tablets are indicated in adult and pediatric patients, including neonates, as a replacement therapy in primary (thyroidal), secondary (pituitary), and tertiary (hypothalamic) congenital or acquired hypothyroidism. Levothyroxine sodium tablets are indicated in adult and pediatric patients, including neonates, as an adjunct to surgery and radioiodine therapy in the management of thyrotropin-dependent well-differentiated thyroid cancer. Levothyroxine sodium tablets are not indicated for suppression of benign thyroid nodules and nontoxic diffuse goiter in iodine-sufficient patients... Levothyroxine sodium tablets are not indicated for treatment of hypothyroidism during the recovery phase of subacute thyroiditis."
