  "adult_dosage": {
    "value": "Administer once daily on an empty stomach one-half to one hour before breakfast with a full glass of water; starting dose individualized by age, body weight, cardiovascular status and concomitant medications; titrate until clinically euthyroid and serum TSH returns to normal; peak therapeutic effect may take 4–6 weeks. Administer at least 4 hours before or after drugs that interfere with absorption.",
    "source_quote": "Administer once daily, preferably on an empty stomach, one-half to one hour before breakfast with a full glass of water. Starting dose depends on a variety of factors, including age, body weight, cardiovascular status, and concomitant medications. Peak therapeutic effect may not be attained for 4 to 6 weeks. For adult patients with primary hypothyroidism, titrate until the patient is clinically euthyroid and the serum TSH returns to normal. Administer levothyroxine sodium tablets at least 4 hours before or after drugs known to interfere with levothyroxine sodium absorption."
  },
  "pediatric_dosage": {
    "value": "Indicated in pediatric patients including neonates. Dosing individualized by age, body weight and clinical status. For children who cannot swallow tablets, crush and suspend freshly crushed tablet in 5–10 mL water and administer immediately by spoon or dropper; ensure full ingestion and do not store the suspension. Do not administer in foods that decrease absorption (e.g., soybean-based infant formula).",
    "source_quote": "Levothyroxine sodium tablets are indicated in adult and pediatric patients, including neonates... The dosage of levothyroxine sodium tablets for hypothyroidism or pituitary TSH suppression depends on a variety of factors including: the patient's age, body weight... Administer levothyroxine sodium tablets to pediatric patients who cannot swallow intact tablets by crushing the tablet, suspending the freshly crushed tablet in a small amount (5 to 10 mL) of water and immediately administering the suspension by spoon or dropper. Ensure the patient ingests the full amount of the suspension. Do not store the suspension. Do not administer in foods that decrease absorption of levothyroxine sodium tablets, such as soybean-based infant formula."
