    "source_quote": "Administer levothyroxine sodium tablets at least 4 hours before or after drugs known to interfere with levothyroxine sodium absorption. Evaluate the need for dosage adjustments when regularly administering within one hour of certain foods that may affect levothyroxine sodium tablets absorption. Advise patients to stop biotin and biotin-containing supplements at least 2 days before assessing TSH and/or T4 levels. Do not administer in foods that decrease absorption of levothyroxine sodium tablets, such as soybean-based infant formula."
